Changelog: 15-11-2026 03:22:26

Fixed. The uninstall on a computer where the app is not installed says so ("… is not installed: nothing to remove.")
and stops, without asking for the sudo password; it listed its removal steps for what was never there (owner,
15-11-2026). With anything of the app there, it uninstalls as before.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 02:03:59

Fixed. The app looks for its newer releases under the suite's tags, bc250-btpair-v<x.y.z> (owner, 15-11-2026: the
BC250 Bazzite Suite's tags start with bc250-).

Changelog: 14-11-2026 23:58:33

Fixed. The suite is a repository of its own, github.com/RobertoTorino/bc250-bazzite (owner, 14-11-2026). The app's
links name it: its releases, its source and its chapter in the wiki, now at robertotorino.github.io/bc250-bazzite/.
From a checkout, its install.sh takes core from core/ at the repository's root, one folder up from before. Nothing
else works differently.

Changelog: 12-11-2026 14:51:59

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 12-11-2026 13:24:26

Added. Escape closes the window, as its close button does, and so does B on a controller (owner, 12-11-2026: inside
the apps the B button and the Escape key exit the app, as they exit the portal): an open menu first, then a question
or a dialog, then the window. A key the window takes for itself comes first, and a window that is busy still asks
before it closes. B is read with pygame-ce from the suite's venv, only while the app has the focus and has had it for
half a second, so the press that closed another app does not close this one too; without pygame-ce or a controller
there is Escape alone. __main__ calls core's exit_keys's install().

